From 62ee8261da3de963d7126a2d1dc1e42772e20bd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Gonzalez Martin <sergiog@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:21:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Backport 8-bit predictive lossless JPEG decoding

Backport Rust-source changes from zune-image PR516:
https://github.com/etemesi254/zune-image/pull/516
Upstream head: f7d10ff8e5e80dd23b2d43f14f49b21a3982bd17
Upstream base: ba9fc2448b71ae1e23268d9d0f404816ac869abe

Support 8-bit grayscale and full-resolution interleaved YCbCr/RGB
predictive lossless JPEG through decode() and decode_into(). Decode
Huffman SOF3 and, with arith enabled, arithmetic SOF11. Preserve predictors,
point transforms, component/table/scan ordering, restart contexts,
incremental replay and packed output bounds.

Preserve reconstructed RGB samples, channel order and opaque alpha for
RGB/BGR/RGBA/BGRA output, including Adobe APP14 ColorTransform=0 input.
Reject unsupported RGB conversions before writing output.

Reuse the QM engine with lossless-specific residual contexts, conditioning
and restart resets. Reject other precisions, sampled/split-scan color and
DNL. Raw and scanline lossless output remain unsupported.

Retain the PR498 Scaled-output rejection and withhold lossless raw
component metadata so Skia does not advertise unsupported YUV decoding.
Keep PR525's configured block converter for YCbCr output.

Keep the rc2 package/version and the preceding thirteen maintained patches,
including PR534's final-input recovery. Apply the PR516-owned changes,
not unrelated changes inherited from its rebased upstream base.
